@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://www.glossarist.org/dpp/dataset/dpp/concept/dpp-0136>
  a skos:Concept ;
  skos:notation "dpp-0136" ;
  skos:prefLabel "blind edge"@eng ;
  skos:definition "edge on a typed passport relationship whose existence and endpoints are concealed from all observers, so that a child-to-parent reference does not reveal where a thing is — a household or a site"@eng ;
  skos:scopeNote "Edge visibility classes — public, restricted (role-qualified), blind and escrowed — are declared on every relationship; the installation schema (concept dpp-0142) carries visibility as an edge class with escrow arrangement (concept dpp-0137) and audiences."@eng ;
  skos:scopeNote "Blind is the default for consumer installations, because even the object-to-household linkage is personal data requiring a GDPR or PIPL legal basis per profile."@eng ;
  skos:scopeNote "Rationale: a traversable graph with entitled upstream observers is surveillance infrastructure; post-sale visibility into instance state is owner-push or authority-based, never maker-pull."@eng
 .